\u003e,\n\u003e or mute the thread\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAOkp1Uiaw_WgUOkHUUPQvg6YEiE5x8mks5uGi5mgaJpZM4Uhmiq\u003e\n\u003e .\n\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531770886,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTM2MTY5Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405361697"},"message":"I was about to hack up a workaround in datalad, but could not find a reliable indicator of Mays/mingw/...another  which would tell us that argument was tempered. So may be then we should just educate our windows users about this feature is the Shell they use and prepend one more /?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531835367,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTU4ODU2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405588563"},"message":"Counter-argument to my suggestion would be non-portability of analysis scripts which have installation steps, e.g. our http://datalad.org/asciicast/reproducible_analysis.sh where there is `datalad install ///...` calls are used.\nThat is because while still in the shell (i.e. also in bash scripts), MSYS does not do any paths mapping:\n![gkrellshoot_07-17-18_093850](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/39889/42820927-58f92ea2-89a5-11e8-99fe-065196ba104f.png)\nSo I thought back that we are doomed to do some analysis, including consideration of the MSYS_NO_PATHCONV variable and adjust any command line argument to not do it, **but** then I have ran into another blow:\n![gkrellshoot_07-17-18_094431](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/39889/42821226-13439860-89a6-11e8-9646-022fc7e798ce.png)\nso, with their mapping there is no way (in the future, since not supported ATM as above exception shows) to distinguish between `///x/y` and `//x/y`  which is a boomer and IMHO was a wrong design on their part in MSYSes.\nSo I am not yet sure what should we do besides ATM warning whenever detecting MSYS system above and considering any url/path provided with leading // .  Or any other ideas @chrisfilo @mih @kyleam ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531844243,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTY0MDc0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405640749"},"message":"regarding the location... all the path mangling madness... try\n```\nls '\\c\\Users\\me\\Downloads\\datalad_test\\ds000002'\n```\n(quotes are important!) ;-)  or \n```\nls /c/c/Users/...\n```\nI guess somewhere our paths manipulations get all deranged and use `\\` convention (start from the root of the drive?) while including the drive letter instead of `/` convention (includes the drive?).  Seems to function a bit more consistent if you use conventional Windows paths or specify paths explicitly.  @mih - does this somehow resonate with your Windows paths \"experiences\"?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1531846931,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTY1NDU4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405654587"},"message":"Paths are tricky, and oyr setup is convoluted (at best). I created an issue on path handling a few weeks ago ( no ref right now, sorry). Conclusion was to abandon all platform path handling and go plain posix internally, converting UNC paths and DOS paths on the way into datalad.\n\nAlso grep for unixifypaths or something similar, which is another contraption that makes life difficult on windows. I assume this was written without considering UNC paths as an option.\n\n/braindump","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531850354,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTY3MTc4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405671783"},"message":"ok, for now fixing up all this sacrificing that unused feature of `//[remote]/` on those windows system for now. PR will come","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1531855338,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwNTY5ODI4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2643#issuecomment-405698288"},"message":"re paths issue: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2546  so let's indeed leave any comments there if any ;-)","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1532113041,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTc0NTQ3NDI5MA=="},"status":2}]}